          <p>
            Single-serving packets and sample sachets are an even cheaper experiment where you can find them; several brands, Clean Simple Eats among them, sell stick packs or single servings. Buying three or four flavors in sachet form before committing to a tub is the most reliable way to avoid a cupboard full of half-finished powders.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where you buy matters too. Our batch-mate guides to <a href="/best-target-protein-powder/">Target protein powder</a> and <a href="/best-walmart-protein-powder/">Walmart protein powder</a> cover what those stores stock in small sizes, and both stores make returns easier than many online marketplaces. Prices on this page move constantly, so treat every figure as a snapshot and check the listing in front of you.
          </p>
